  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two multimodal experiments (config_013: avgpool+concat, acc=0.715; config_047: transformer+concat, acc=0.721) show that aggregation method has negligible impact (~0.006 difference) when using scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + concat fusion. The image-only baseline (0.332) confirms RNA is essential. The key untested variable in the current best setup is the fusion method (weighted vs concat). Question: config_043 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly extends the best result (config_047) by swapping concat for weighted fusion, testing whether learned per-modality weighting can further improve accuracy beyond 0.721. Why this is the best next step: With 6 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest evidence (the exact encoder/profile combination that already yields ~0.72) by testing the one untried architectural knob (fusion) is the highest-information, lowest-risk move. It avoids the large uncertainty of switching RNA or image encoders while directly probing whether we can push past the current plateau. Expected cost: ~4.6–4.7 GPU hours, comparable to config_047, since the architecture (same encoders, transformer aggregation) is identical."
}

